# Paths reqmap should not scan (one fnmatch glob per line, # comments ok).
# scripts/reqmap.py is intentionally NOT ignored: this repo hosts its own
# requirements there (its membership tags resolve to local requirements), so
# the engine must stay scanned. Add other vendored/generated paths below.
# The bundled single-file viewer is a generated artifact, never a member.
scripts/_map_viewer.html

# --- excalidraw-diagram skill ---
# SKILL.md: classified as 'ignore' bucket by REQ-PROSE-024 (user contract, not
# a capability implementation).
skills/excalidraw-diagram/SKILL.md
# examples/: transient generators — correctness proved by test_excalidraw.py.
# A new example should not require a new requirement.
skills/excalidraw-diagram/examples/*.py
# references/: Excalidraw JSON format reference doc — not a capability.
skills/excalidraw-diagram/references/excalidraw_format.md

# --- requirement-manager skill ---
# SKILL.md: same 'ignore' bucket classification. The engine's own skill
# contract is described by requirements in plugin/requirements/, not by
# tagging SKILL.md itself.
skills/requirement-manager/SKILL.md

# --- working docs / specs ---
# Design specs and superpowers working notes under docs/ are sync_only prose
# (REQ-PROSE-024 bucket), not capability implementations.
docs/superpowers/specs/*.md

# --- app/ and repo-root scripts/ ---
# app/ (Vite+React viewer source) and scripts/check_versions.py live at the
# repo root — OUTSIDE plugin/'s scan root. They carry no implements: tags by
# design: the viewer UX is tested via npm build; the version-gate script is
# dev-CI tooling described in CLAUDE.md and cross-referenced in REQ-CHECK-006.
# No ignore entry needed here (structural scope already excludes them) — this
# comment exists solely to document the intent so future contributors don't
# wonder why these files have no tags.
